[Music]  when the Mercedes SL debuted in 1963 it  had a tough act to follow  it was meant to be sporty but elegant  comfortable but fast all with the  familiar mercedes-benz quality and  reliability the SL was all that and  today as a classy car it still is it  swiftly acquired the nickname pagoda for  its concave hardtop mercedes-benz  presented its new SL series at the  Geneva International Motor Show as the  successor to both the legendary 300 SL  and the 190 SL known internally by its  chassis code w113 it was no domesticated  race car but more a sporty two-seater  car for street driving  [Music]  the pagoda was a hit especially in the  United States more than half the cars  produced were sold to America the ladies  were also charmed by this easy-to-handle  roadster  another reason for its appeal was the  new design vocabulary the w113 heralded  the demise of the Baroque contours of  its Mercedes forerunners and the advent  of sporty-er masculine lines while  preserving Mercedes typically genteel  elegance it was thoroughly modern but  not trendy the hardtop was standard on  every SL the roofs nicknamed pagoda  quickly evolved into a term of  endearment for the whole car in 1963 the  new Mercedes drew a lot of attention a  young French designer Paul Brock created  the new look and Mercedes design  language for the decade to come Mercedes  experts Multan lingonberry explains that  Paul Brock preferred graceful lines  compared to its predecessors the 300 SL  and 190 SL roadsters he very nearly  designed a compact car it was in fact a  compact sedan but had its own unique  style that seemed to glide along with  ease described in first poems the top up  or down the convertible cut a good  figure it's interior sacrifice another  Mercedes trademark opulence ease and  comfort  [Music]  the optional four-speed automatic  transmission was very popular with  buyers  [Music]  even if Mercedes gave the model a touch  of sportiness nowadays connoisseurs  appreciate the pagoda more for leisurely  drives and outings in the country  [Music]  now a pagoda in good condition will  fetch at least 60,000 euros the later  280s  were the most well engineered the  Mercedes 280 SL pagoda may not have been  as exciting as its Italian and American  competitors but it was robust and  reliable  [Music]

